            <div xml:id="d203">

                <pb facs="0494" n="398" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg398"/>

                <head>No. 182.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. White to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-09-09"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 9, 1879</date>.
                        (Received September 24.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 48.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your instruction No. 7 of the
                    23d of May last, calling for certain information for the Secretary of the
                    Treasury, respecting the amount of gold and silver coin and bullion and paper
                    currency in Germany, I have the honor to state that the legation applied to the
                    imperial foreign office for the information desired, on the 17th of June last,
                    and that a reply, under date of the 30th ultimo, has been received to its
                    communication.</p>
                <p>Copies of this correspondence, as well as copies of the inclosures accompanying
                    the foreign office note, together with translations of such of them as are not
                    in print, are herewith inclosed.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>AND. D. WHITE.</signed></closer>





